From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:15:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] settings: IFS firmware switch on Kiln's API, with the owner's
 opt-in

The previous patch's Settings > Devices > IFS firmware moves onto Kiln
OS's API: Moonraker's kiln_os component answers
machine.kiln_os.get_ifs_firmware (GET /machine/kiln_os/ifs_firmware:
available, enabled, firmware, state idle/running/done/failed, target,
phase, reason, message, version) also while Klipper is stopped, and
machine.kiln_os.post_ifs_firmware (POST with target stock or klipper)
hands the switch to Kiln's update agent, which answers at once and
switches in the background. Klipper's ifs_firmware object and
/server/kiln/ifs_firmware are gone.

The row shows only where Kiln says the switch is available (the owner
turned it on; subject ad5x_ifs_firmware_available). Without that,
"Switch to Klipper" never shows; the way back to stock does. Kiln's
object is fetched in the discovery sequence (every connect and Klipper
restart), when Settings opens and when the overlay opens.

The model, not the overlay, follows a switch: while one runs (also one
started elsewhere) or Klipper is not back after one this screen asked
for, it asks Kiln once a second and holds off the recovery dialog
("Printer shutdown", "Klipper disconnected"), also with the overlay
closed. The hold-off ends at once when Klipper reports an error after
the switch, and after 180 s without Klipper. A refusal shows Kiln's
reason without its "[reason]" prefix (refusal_text). One request at a
time.

After a request the hardware check no longer skips its whole notice
for 10 minutes: only IFS objects (mcu ifs, ifs_*, Happy Hare's mmu*,
is_ifs_hardware) are left out of it; other changes are still notified.

The confirm and result texts say what happens now: Klipper stops for 1
to 4 minutes, and on stock firmware a plugin that needs Klipper firmware
on the IFS is skipped until the switch back (Kiln no longer turns it
off). Strings in translations/en.yml and ru.yml.

HELIX_KILN_AD5X builds only; elsewhere nothing is asked and the row
stays hidden.

Tests: the view (each phase, the replug hint, done and failed texts, a
refusal also while Klipper is away, the choice with and without the
opt-in, during a print, a switch started elsewhere, the wait limits),
is_ifs_hardware, Kiln's object read field by field; the model: the row
only where Kiln offers the switch, nothing asked off Kiln or without a
connection, an older Kiln without the method, a whole switch (the POST,
a second tap ignored, polls with the overlay closed, the hold-off, the
result once Klipper is back, OK), a refusal, Klipper's error after the
switch ending the hold-off, a switch started elsewhere. The new overlay
goes in the toolhead-safety census (test_job_holds_machine.cpp) as one
that commands no motion.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
